"roman":"xu"},{"t":"ख़ि","parts":["ख़","ि"],"roman":"xi"}]},{"id":"hi-ghha","st":"deva","set":8,"group":"nukta","t":"ग़","name":"ġa","roman":"ġa","alt":["ġ"],"say":"ग़","note":"ġ, a throaty g like French r","confuse":["hi-ga"],"ex":[["w0250","ġalat"]]},{"id":"hi-ao","st":"deva","set":8,"group":"vowel","t":"ऑ","name":"ŏ","roman":"ŏ","alt":["aw"],"say":"ऑ","note":"o as in British 'hot' (English words): ऑफ़िस ŏfis","confuse":["hi-o","hi-au"],"ex":[["w1076","ŏfis"]]},{"id":"hi-m-ao","st":"deva","set":8,"group":"matra","t":"ॉ","name":"ŏ kī mātrā","roman":"ŏ","alt":["aw"],"say":"कॉ","note":"the ŏ sign, a moon over the o sign: डॉक्टर ḍŏkṭar, कॉलेज kŏlej","confuse":["hi-m-o","hi-m-au"],"ex":[["w0467","ḍŏkṭar"],["w2004","kŏlej"]],"syll":[{"t":"डॉ","parts":["ड","ॉ"],"roman":"ḍŏ"},{"t":"कॉ","parts":["क","ॉ"],"roman":"kŏ"}],"base":"hi-ao"},{"id":"hi-nga","st":"deva","set":9,"group":"velar","t":"ङ","name":"ṅa","roman":"ṅa","alt":["ṅ"],"say":"ङ","note":"ng as in 'sing' (rare)","confuse":["hi-dda"]},{"id":"hi-nya","st":"deva","set":9,"group":"palatal","t":"ञ","name":"ña","roman":"ña","alt":["ñ"],"say":"ञ","note":"ny (rare)","confuse":["hi-ja"]},{"id":"hi-visarga","st":"deva","set":9,"group":"sign","t":"ः","name":"visarg","roman":"ḥ","alt":["h"],"say":"अः","note":"a light h after a vowel: दुःख duḥkh","confuse":["hi-virama"],"ex":[["w0772","duḥkh"]]},{"id":"hi-ksa","st":"deva","set":10,"group":"conjunct","t":"क्ष","name":"kṣa","roman":"kṣa","alt":["ksh"],"say":"क्ष","note":"k + ṣ: क्षमा kṣamā","confuse":["hi-ka","hi-tra"],"ex":[["w0229","kṣetra"],["w0320","surakṣā"],["w0398","surakṣit"]],"syll":[{"t":"क्षा","parts":["क्ष","ा"],"roman":"kṣā"},{"t":"क्षे","parts":["क्ष","े"],"roman":"kṣe"},{"t":"क्षि","parts":["क्ष","ि"],"roman":"kṣi"}]},{"id":"hi-tra","st":"deva","set":10,"group":"conjunct","t":"त्र","name":"tra","roman":"tra","alt":["tr"],"say":"त्र","note":"t + r: मित्र mitra","confuse":["hi-ta","hi-ksa"],"ex":[["w0229","kṣetra"],["w0404","mantrī"],["w0417","chātra"]],"syll":[{"t":"त्री","parts":["त्र","ी"],"roman":"trī"}]},{"id":"hi-jna","st":"deva","set":10,"group":"conjunct","t":"ज्ञ","name":"jña","roman":"jña","alt":["gya"],"say":"ज्ञ","note":"j + ñ, said gy: ज्ञान jñān","confuse":["hi-ja","hi-sra"],"ex":[["w0609","jñān"],["w0987","vijñān"],["w1110","vaijñānik"]]},{"id":"hi-sra","st":"deva","set":10,"group":"conjunct","t":"श्र","name":"śra","roman":"śra","alt":["shr"],"say":"श्र","note":"ś + r: श्री śrī","confuse":["hi-sha","hi-jna"],"ex":[["w0692","śrīmān"]]},{"id":"hi-dya","st":"deva","set":10,"group":"conjunct","t":"द्य","name":"dya","roman":"dya","alt":["dy"],"say":"द्य","note":"d + y: विद्या vidyā","confuse":["hi-da","hi-dva"],"ex":[["w1044","viśvavidyālay"],["w1207","udyog"]]},{"id":"hi-dva","st":"deva","set":10,"group":"conjunct","t":"द्व","name":"dva","roman":"dva","alt":["dv"],"say":"द्व","note":"d + v: द्वार dvār","confuse":["hi-da","hi-dya"],"ex":[["w0129","dvārā"]],"syll":[{"t":"द्वा","parts":["द्व","ा"],"roman":"dvā"}]}],"notes":[{"st":"deva","set":1,"h":"The inherent a","body":"Every consonant letter carries a short a: क is ka. A vowel sign (mātrā) replaces it: का kā. At the end of a word the a is usually silent: नाम nām, not nāma."},{"st":"deva","set":2,"h":"ि comes first","body":"The short i sign is written before its consonant but read after it: कि ki, दिन din."},{"st":"deva","set":3,"h":"Halant and half letters","body":"् removes the inherent a. Usually the first consonant of a cluster is written as a half letter joined to the next: क्या kyā, बच्चा baccā, प्यार pyār."},{"st":"deva","set":3,"h":"रु and रू","body":"With र the u signs sit beside the letter, not below it: रु ru (गुरु guru), रू rū (रूप rūp). Compare कु ku and कू kū."},{"st":"deva","set":3,"h":"र in clusters","body":"र before a consonant becomes a small hook above the next letter (reph): कर्म karm, दर्द dard. र after a consonant becomes a slanted stroke at its foot (rakar): प्रेम prem, ग्राम grām; त + र is written त्र."},{"st":"deva","set":4,"h":"Nasal vowels","body":"ँ (chandrabindu) and ं (bindu) make the vowel nasal: हाँ hā̃, में mẽ, नहीं nahī̃. Before a consonant ं is an n or m sound: हिंदी hindī, कंबल kambal. Many writers use ं for both."},{"st":"deva","set":5,"h":"Aspirated letters","body":"ख घ थ ध फ भ छ झ are single sounds with a puff of air: kh is k + breath, not k + h. Hold a hand in front of your mouth to feel it."},{"st":"deva","set":6,"h":"Retroflex and dental","body":"ट ठ ड ढ ण are said with the tongue curled back; त थ द ध न with the tongue on the teeth. English t and d sit between the two."},{"st":"deva","set":8,"h":"The nukta dot","body":"A dot below changes the sound: ड़ ṛ and ढ़ ṛh are flapped r sounds (बड़ा, पढ़ना); ज़ z, फ़ f, क़ q, ख़ x, ग़ ġ are used in Persian, Arabic and English words. Many writers leave the dot out."},{"st":"deva","set":9,"h":"ङ and ञ","body":"ङ and ञ appear in older and Sanskrit spellings before a consonant of their own group: अङ्ग, पञ्च. Modern spelling uses ं instead: अंग aṅg, पंच pañc."},{"st":"deva","set":10,"h":"Conjunct shapes","body":"Most clusters are half letters, but a few have shapes of their own: क्ष kṣ, त्र tr, ज्ञ gy, श्र śr, द्य dy, द्व dv. Learn them as single letters."}]}
